course: dictionary
lesson: 1509
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word cell is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «The first living things on Earth were tiny single cells in the sea.» The clues are tiny, living things and sea, so here a cell is the smallest living part of a plant or animal.
explain: Now look at «In 2020 a Przewalski's horse foal called Kurt was cloned from cells frozen 40 years earlier.» Cloned and foal are about living animals, so cells means the living parts that make up a body. A cell in a prison means something very different, so the clues decide the meaning every time.
explain: Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence? Then try it in place of the word. If «a tiny living part» fits, you have found it. If you read «a small room» and the sentence makes no sense, try a different meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cell» means the smallest living part of a plant or animal, and all living things are made of cells.
fact: «Cell» can also mean a small room where a prisoner is kept, or a battery that makes electricity.
fact: In maths and computing, «cell» means one small box in a table or spreadsheet.
fact: In American English, «cell» can mean a mobile phone, so «cell phone» is the same as a mobile.
exercise: In «The first living things on Earth were tiny single cells in the sea», what is a cell? | A box in a table | *The smallest living part of a plant or animal | A small room with bars | A battery that makes electricity
exercise: Which clue in «cloned from cells frozen 40 years earlier» tells you cells are living parts, not prison rooms? | Frozen | 2020 | Earlier | *Cloned from a living horse foal
exercise: An American says, «My cell is dead, I need to charge it.» What does cell mean? | A battery | A prison room | *A mobile phone | A box in a spreadsheet
test: In «You smell cookies because tiny bits float up your nose and land on smell cells that tell your brain», what does cells mean? | A small room | A battery | *Tiny living parts of your body | A box in a table
test: Which meaning of cell fits a row and column of boxes on a screen? | A mobile phone | *One small box in a table or spreadsheet | A living part of a plant | A prison room
exam: Which phrase uses cell to mean a small room where a prisoner is kept? | plant cell | solar cell | blood cells | *prison cell
